Report a StartThread entry the recompiler did not emit as a [guest-branch:missing-target]
(from a copy of the caller's context), as the EE scheduler does, so the learning run adds it.
The OSD's XDEV9 loader thread entry is only address-taken; StartThread refused it silently and
the boot waited on its semaphore forever.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/Thread.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/Thread.cpp
@@ -272,6 +272,11 @@ namespace ps2_syscalls
         }
         if (!runtime->hasFunction(target->entry))
         {
+            // Report the entry the recompiler missed (often only address-taken), as the
+            // scheduler does, so it is learned instead of the thread silently never running.
+            R5900Context report = *ctx; // the report retargets pc; the caller keeps its own
+            runtime->reportMissingFunction(rdram, &report, target->entry, ctx->pc,
+                                           PS2Runtime::GuestBranchKind::DirectCall, "StartThread");
             setReturnS32(ctx, KE_ERROR);
             return;
         }
